101
00:12:45.933 --> 00:12:50.696
<v Daniel>Well, the audit flagged 15 out of the 91 final red lines for possible AI use.</v>

102
00:12:50.936 --> 00:12:52.096
<v Maya>Wow, 15.</v>

103
00:12:52.316 --> 00:12:59.820
<v Daniel>Yeah, but here's the key. Even when they statistically controlled for those flag cases, the core findings absolutely held up.</v>

104
00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:03.281
<v Maya>Okay, that's solid. But we should be honest with the listener about the limits here.</v>

105
00:13:03.421 --> 00:13:03.861
<v Daniel>Definitely.</v>

106
00:13:04.022 --> 00:13:17.415
<v Maya>This was a pretty small sample. 91 people completed the full protocol. The firms were heavily selected through a sophisticated client, Google. The experiment was funded by Google. It used a Google tool and had mostly Google co-authors.</v>

107
00:13:17.881 --> 00:13:23.684
<v Daniel>All right. There's a lot of Google in there. Also, the partner firms absolutely refused to do a baseline skills test.</v>

108
00:13:23.864 --> 00:13:25.165
